    {
      "latin": "pilam mittere",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "throw the ball to someone: pass it",
      "grammar": "mittō, mittere, mīsī, missum, with pilam; the receiver with ad + acc. or the dative",
      "evidence": [
        "Sen. Ben. 2.17.4: <span lang=\"la\">audācius pilam mittēmus</span>; <span lang=\"la\">aliter illam conlūsōrī longō, aliter brevī mittat</span>"
      ],
      "comment": "Seneca’s phrase, after Chrysippus, for the throw from one player to another in a game of catch; the plain classical way to say “pass it” in any ball game."
    }
